A||||15||MISTER_PORKY||Power Steering ?||||1||
Z||000000||MISTER_PORKY||09-21-2001||12:57 AM||||Hi gang !<BR>  I'm doing my home work to find out all I can about '88 GT'S and Formulas. I was told tonight that these models have electric power assisted steering. Is this true ? I've never heard this before. Also did these cars come standard with vented disc brakes on all 4 corners ? I have an '84, and I know '88's are a whole different breed.<BR>  And can anyone fill me in on the subwoofer option. The basic concept of how it works and the control system layout. Just the basics. Don't need to get technical. I'm just trying to get enough info as to what to look for.<BR>      Thanks !<P>    ~~~ GOD BLESS THE U.S.A ~~~||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ferrari_cdn||09-21-2001||01:56 AM||||If I read correctly, NONE of the fieros come with power steering.  If some of the cars have it, it was the owners who installed it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_2.JPG">  <BR>'84 2m4, 4 speed, 106k miles (157k km)  AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-21-2001||04:42 AM||||Supposedly, 12 '88 Fieros came out with a hydro electric p/s unit, but none were sold the the general public.  Either they were test mules or they're sitting in the back of some GM execs garage.  Rodney Dickman used to have one of the prototype p/s units, I think.  I have no idea what he ever did with it.  <P>'88s have vented discs all around.<P>The sub system was pretty simple if I understand it correctly.  The amp was mounted between the carpet and the center console (up by your feet), the sub (more like a mid, if you ask me) was mounted in a tube of sorts under the passenger side dash and there was a slider control built into the overhead light console.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kasdan||09-21-2001||08:38 AM||||No fiero was every produced with p/s that was meant to be had by the public.  period.  that being said, I have power steering.  I'm not entirely sure about its origion, i do know how its been installed.  There is a resuavor  bolted to the trunk side firewall, and theres a aluminum bracket bolted to the top 2 bolts of the water pump, which the p/s pump is attached to.  i dont know where the steering rack came from.  On a side note, the fiero dosent need power steering at all.  My power steering takes away approx. 15 HP because its a belt driven pump.  when racing or autox-ing, i disconnect the pump.  but for just driving around town, its a god given miracle.  My 86 has the vented rotors all around.  I also have the factory subwoofer option, although when i got my car, the subwoofer and box were gone.  I do have the amp and volume slider, and everything is wired up and ready to go, all i need is the box and a sub and im ready to go!<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">          <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986<p>[This message has been edited by Kasdan (edited 09-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||09-21-2001||09:20 AM||||NO POWER STEERING OPTION FOR A FIERO!<P>The Saginaw system didn't go into production.<P>After market Mercury Merkur hydralic systems were add ons as were any other Fieros with power steering.||||reg||1
Z||000005||skitime||09-21-2001||09:22 AM||||Hey Kasdan, How about some pics of the power steering install.  Pump, reservoir, and rack. Many of us would like to see it.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Kasdan||09-21-2001||09:45 AM||||Skitime - for some reason, when i got my pics developed, the pics of my engine compartment didnt come out.  My camera is broken, and i dont have a digicam, so i cant take pics right now.  Now that i think about it, My car has a thrown rod and is motorless right now, but when i get a new motor, ill be sure to put the power steering back in and take some pics.  might take some time though.  Ronnie has seen it, i have a witness!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">         <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||09-21-2001||10:38 AM||||I've also heard that several (12?) Fieros were built with power steering, but they were converted back to manual before being sold.  The option was pulled at the last minute.  So the bottom line, yes, a very few power steering units do exists, but none were ever available from the factory.  Rodney Dickman has an original power steering unit on his Mera (one he retrofitted - don't know where he got it), so I've heard.||||reg||6
Z||000008||Fformula88||09-21-2001||11:09 AM||||I've also heard, and been contacted by someone who has confirmed thru a lot of research that a low number (I forget the exact, but about 12) were originally produced by GM with the power steering.<P>All Pontiac's 1988 literature indicates that the Fiero's would have power steering as an option by mid year, so they definately pulled the plug on it late!<P>I've heard an updated version of the electric power steering originally designed for the Fiero is going to be used by GM in current cars.  I believe some if not all of the new Saturn SUE or SVE or whatever thwey are calling them is going to use one.  GM is siting increased fuel economy as the reason for putting them into production since they don't have a pump drawing on the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000009||MinnGreenGT||09-21-2001||11:09 AM||||Ok... there were no PS equipped Fieros sold.  none.  As for adding PowerSteering... it can be done.  The system from a Merkur XR4Ti is supposedly a bolt on.  There has also been some speculation about a possible Volvo bolt-on (AUS used a volvo steering set for his RH drive GT).  I saw someone at the Dells run this year with a 3800 conversion running the stock GM PS pump to the Merkur XR4Ti setup. Wish I had some pics or more info...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000010||MISTER_PORKY||09-21-2001||12:48 PM||||Thanks for the replies.<BR>   The reason I asked the question about power steering to start with is this, I found an '88 GT for sale, a two owner car, and was told by the present owner that is has electric power assisted steering. I'm sure it could be an aftermarket setup. but I wasn't sure about a factory option. I haven't seen the car in person yest, so I don't have a clue what this power seering thing is all about ! <BR>   Again, thanks !<P>   ~~~ GOD BLESS THE U.S.A. ~~~||||reg||1
