Z||000012||gusto||09-21-2001||12:54 PM||||I could be wrong but ar'nt asisted steering and power steering different? I was told asisted steering only kicks in at low speeds and power steering works all the time....just a though let me know if i'm wrong.||||reg||5
Z||000013||Monkeyman||09-21-2001||07:12 PM||||Kasdan--If your '86 has vented rotors, they aren't factory.  The only year to get factory vented rotors was '88.  <P>I'm not terribly impressed with vented rotors.  I added the Fiero Stores vented rotors to the front of the Grape Ape and did the Grand Am "upgrade" the the rear.  I also swapped to the Blazer MC and Earls SS brake lines.  I really didn't see *that* much different.  (At least not enough to justify the cost.)  This car will get SS brake lines and rebuilt calipers some day (doesn't need them now), but that's about it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000014||LS1swap||09-21-2001||08:22 PM||||I remember seeing a motor week TV show in which an electric power steering unit was installed I have herd that none were sold with that option. I bet some one in GM knows the whole story. My thinking is that there must of been some problem with the units or they just decided not to implement them after they pulled the plug on the fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Fformula88||09-21-2001||11:34 PM||||I would go check out the car if its advertised with an electric power steering system!  Anything is possible since a factory blue 85 was just found!<P>Who knows, maybe one of the test mules leaked out of GM's hands somehow... it could be a rare vehicle.  Make sure to check for the power steering components too, and that its just not a sales pitch that isn't true!||||reg||1
